"cell_type":"code","source":"data = {\"day_wise\": day_wise, \"full_grouped\": full_grouped}\nbefore = {name: (len(df), df.isna().sum().sum()) for name, df in data.items()}\n\n\n# column names and text values\nfor df in data.values():\n    df.columns = df.columns.str.strip()\n    for col in df.select_dtypes(include=\"object\").columns:\n        df[col] = df[col].str.strip().replace(\"\", np.nan)\n\n\n# dates (print anything that fails to parse)\nfor name, df in data.items():\n    raw = df[\"Date\"]\n    df[\"Date\"] = pd.to_datetime(raw, errors=\"coerce\")\n    bad = df[\"Date\"].isna() & raw.notna()\n    if bad.any():\n        print(f\"{name}: {bad.sum()} dates could not be parsed, e.g. {raw[bad].unique()[:3]}\")\n\n\n# numeric columns (print anything that fails to convert)\nnumeric_cols = {\n    \"day_wise\": [\"Confirmed\", \"Deaths\", \"Recovered\", \"Active\", \"New cases\", \"New deaths\",\n                 \"New recovered\", \"Deaths / 100 Cases\", \"Recovered / 100 Cases\",\n                 \"Deaths / 100 Recovered\", \"No. of countries\"],\n    \"full_grouped\": [\"Confirmed\", \"Deaths\", \"Recovered\", \"Active\",\n                     \"New cases\", \"New deaths\", \"New recovered\"],\n}\n\nfor name, cols in numeric_cols.items():\n    df = data[name]\n    for col in cols:\n        raw = df[col]\n        values = raw.str.replace(\",\", \"\", regex=False) if raw.dtype == object else raw\n        df[col] = pd.to_numeric(values, errors=\"coerce\")\n        bad = df[col].isna() & raw.notna()\n        if bad.any():\n            print(f\"{name}: {bad.sum()} values in {col} could not be converted, e.g. {raw[bad].unique()[:3]}\")\n    df.replace([np.inf, -np.inf], np.nan, inplace=True)\n\n\n# drop rows missing key columns, then exact duplicates only\nkeys = {\"day_wise\": [\"Date\"], \"full_grouped\": [\"Date\", \"Country/Region\"]}\n\nfor name, cols in keys.items():\n    df = data[name]\n    n0 = len(df)\n    df = df.dropna(subset=cols)\n    n1 = len(df)\n    df = df.drop_duplicates().copy()\n    print(f\"{name}: {n0 - n1} rows missing keys, {n1 - len(df)} exact duplicates removed\")\n    data[name] = df\n\n\n# invalid counts: negatives, or deaths/recovered above confirmed\ncum = [\"Confirmed\", \"Deaths\", \"Recovered\"]\n\nfor name, df in data.items():\n    for col in cum:\n        neg = df[col] < 0\n        if neg.any():\n            print(f\"{name}: {neg.sum()} negative values in {col} set to NaN\")\n            df.loc[neg, col] = np.nan\n    for col in [\"Deaths\", \"Recovered\"]:\n        over = df[col] > df[\"Confirmed\"]\n        if over.any():\n            print(f\"{name}: {over.sum()} rows where {col} > Confirmed set to NaN\")\n            df.loc[over, col] = np.nan\n\n    # negative daily values are reporting corrections, so keep them but report them\n    for col in [\"New cases\", \"New deaths\", \"New recovered\"]:\n        n = (df[col] < 0).sum()\n        if n:\n            print(f\"{name}: {n} negative values in {col} (kept)\")\n\n\n# imputation: cumulative totals can't disappear, so carry the last known value forward\ndw = data[\"day_wise\"].sort_values(\"Date\").reset_index(drop=True)\ndw[cum] = dw[cum].ffill()\n\nfg = data[\"full_grouped\"].sort_values([\"Country/Region\", \"Date\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\nfg[cum] = fg.groupby(\"Country/Region\")[cum].ffill()\n\n# recalculate Active, and fix any row where it comes out negative\nfor name, df in ((\"day_wise\", dw), (\"full_grouped\", fg)):\n    df[\"Active\"] = df[\"Confirmed\"] - df[\"Deaths\"] - df[\"Recovered\"]\n    neg = df[\"Active\"] < 0\n    if neg.any():\n        print(f\"{name}: {neg.sum()} rows with negative Active, Recovered capped at Confirmed minus Deaths\")\n        show = [c for c in [\"Country/Region\", \"Date\", \"Confirmed\", \"Deaths\", \"Recovered\"] if c in df.columns]\n        print(df.loc[neg, show].to_string(index=False))\n        df.loc[neg, \"Recovered\"] = df.loc[neg, \"Confirmed\"] - df.loc[neg, \"Deaths\"]\n        df.loc[neg, \"Active\"] = 0\n    df[cum + [\"Active\"]] = df[cum + [\"Active\"]].astype(\"int64\")\n\n\n# recompute rate columns so they match the cleaned counts\ndw[\"Deaths / 100 Cases\"] = (dw[\"Deaths\"] / dw[\"Confirmed\"] * 100).round(2)\ndw[\"Recovered / 100 Cases\"] = (dw[\"Recovered\"] / dw[\"Confirmed\"] * 100).round(2)\ndw[\"Deaths / 100 Recovered\"] = (dw[\"Deaths\"] / dw[\"Recovered\"] * 100).round(2)\ndw.replace([np.inf, -np.inf], np.nan, inplace=True)\n\n\n# check that day_wise has one row for every day\ngaps = (dw[\"Date\"].diff().dt.days > 1).sum()\nprint(f\"day_wise: {gaps} gaps in dates\")\n\ndata[\"day_wise\"], data[\"full_grouped\"] = dw, fg\n\n\nsummary = pd.DataFrame(\n    [[*before[n], len(df), df.isna().sum().sum()] for n, df in data.items()],\n    index=data.keys(),\n    columns=[\"rows before\", \"NaN before\", \"rows after\", \"NaN after\"],\n)\nprint(\"\\n\", summary)\n\nfor name, df in data.items():\n    missing = df.isna().sum()\n    missing = missing[missing > 0]\n    if not missing.empty:\n        print(f\"\\nMissing values in {name}\\n{missing}\")\n\nday_wise, full_grouped = dw, fg","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T09:02:26.080249Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T09:02:26.080565Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T09:02:26.258952Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-18T09:02:26.080538Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T09:02:26.258008Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"day_wise: 0 rows missing keys, 0 exact duplicates removed\nfull_grouped: 0 rows missing keys, 0 exact duplicates removed\nfull_grouped: 1 rows where Recovered > Confirmed set to NaN\nfull_grouped: 38 negative values in New deaths (kept)\nfull_grouped: 77 negative values in New recovered (kept)\nfull_grouped: 1 rows with negative Active, Recovered capped at Confirmed minus Deaths\nCountry/Region       Date  Confirmed  Deaths  Recovered\n Liechtenstein 2020-06-23         82       2       81.0\nday_wise: 0 gaps in dates\n\n               rows before  NaN before  rows after  NaN after\nday_wise              188           0         188          0\nfull_grouped        35156           0       35156          0\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":98},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"*The cleaning checked column names, text values, dates and numeric columns. No rows had missing key values and no exact duplicates were found. In full_grouped, one row for Liechtenstein on 23 June 2020 had more recoveries than confirmed cases. Its recoveries were first filled with the previous day's value and then capped at confirmed minus deaths, so active cases did not go below zero. Negative daily values for new deaths (38) and new recoveries (77) were kept, since they are reporting corrections. Active cases were recalculated from the cleaned counts, and the day wise data has no missing dates.*","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Global COVID-19 Statistics**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"print(\"Global COVID Statistics\")\nprint(\"Total Confirmed Cases:\", day_wise[\"Confirmed\"].max())\nprint(\"Total Deaths:\", day_wise[\"Deaths\"].max())\nprint(\"Total Recovered:\", day_wise[\"Recovered\"].max())\nprint(\"Maximum Active Cases:\", day_wise[\"Active\"].max())","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T09:02:26.260614Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T09:02:26.260926Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T09:02:26.268025Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-18T09:02:26.260896Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T09:02:26.267059Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Global COVID Statistics\nTotal Confirmed Cases: 16480485\nTotal Deaths: 654036\nTotal Recovered: 9468087\nMaximum Active Cases: 6358362\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":99},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"*By 27 July 2020 there were 16,480,485 confirmed cases worldwide, with 654,036 deaths and 9,468,087 recoveries. Active cases peaked at 6,358,362, which shows how man